 ## Background
-The concept was introduced in the thesis "Skalierbares Webbasiertes Volume Rendering großer biomedizinischer Datensätze" [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes between the resolution levels of a volume and the spatial, purely geometric subdivision determined by the residency octree [S1, unofficial]. The work builds on previous research, such as that by Hadwiger et al. [HBJP12], regarding flexible downsampling ratios [S1, unofficial].
-
+The concept originates from the work on scalable web-based volume rendering of large biomedical datasets [S1, unofficial]. It distinguishes the resolution levels of a volume from the spatial, purely geometric subdivision determined by a residency octree [S1, unofficial]. This separation allows for flexible downsampling ratios between resolution levels, contrasting with the fixed halving subdivision of octree nodes [S1, unofficial].
